invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64_addcarry.c
catches: rsa_addcarry_equiv_test
reason: block_mul_add's chain starts from zero in place of w, the carry
  word of the block below, so every block but a row's first loses the
  carry the one below it handed up. bin/rsa_addcarry_equiv_test runs the
  rows under any compiler and compares their words with rsa_mont64.c's
  loops.

--- old
    unsigned char carry = add_carry(0, (addcarry_word)q0, w, &t[0]);
--- new
    unsigned char carry = add_carry(0, (addcarry_word)q0, w & 0, &t[0]);
